From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 19:56:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07712/11362] [outer-loop] ARC overcorrection fix: neutral
 frame when no mover (marginal, REQ-ARC-WMTE-5834)

reauthor_framing now uses a neutral options frame (move-to-target / arrange-merge /
satisfy-pattern) when NO mover is detected, instead of forcing navigation. Result:
4 correct / 3 partial / 1 wrong (vs forced-navigate 4/2/2) -- lf52 moved wrong->partial,
but ft09 stayed wrong. gemma defaults to "reach an object" even with neutral options;
the deeper limit is the detector can't infer game TYPE (navigate/merge/CSP). The 4
navigate wins are stable. 15 unit tests. v1 (committed) preserved; v2 saved distinctly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
---
